{"parentUuid":"41463587-dfff-4545-9ddb-9a45573c0665","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgt3ofJAfTfFzZEhSLCox","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job page is committed as `1f589d6`, which is local and not pushed. The earlier pages were pushed (`338a861..dc15a41`).\n\n**What it has:**\n- The request and its badges. The issue and pull-request badges open in your browser.\n- The failure box.\n- **The wait:**\n  - The agent's question, and a line on what Approve does at this step.\n  - The report being judged, and the diff. Clicking a diff line adds `file:line: ` to the note.\n  - Approve, Send back or Answer, and Stop.\n- The calls the gate holds, with Allow once and Refuse with a note.\n- The charter.\n- The workflow drawn on an iced canvas, each step marked with its state, and the step results.\n- The steps, each opening to its artifacts and the latest turn.\n\n**Checks:** the client has 21 tests, clippy is clean, and CodeScene passes. CodeScene now skips one rule in `pages/drawing.rs`, the limit on function arguments. iced's canvas trait requires `draw` to take six arguments, and the rules file says why.\n\n**Not seen live:** I haven't seen the job page on screen. The stack is still stopped, so the server can't read any job. The Jobs page drew, but it showed no jobs.\n\n**Still to port in G2:** Workflows (the editable canvas, the largest page), Constraints, Capabilities, the Audit Log, Evals, Engine and Settings.\n\nBefore the next page, may I start the stack again? Without it I can't check any page against real data."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":518875,"output_tokens":680,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":186},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_toke